From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Domenico D'Arrigo <DCHEM88@hotmail.it>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 09:55:42 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] soc/intel/cannonlake: Let an option turn the HD Audio
 controller off

FSP-M enables the HD Audio controller from the devicetree, so a
mainboard can only offer to turn it off at build time: the devicetree
of ramstage comes too late. Read the "onboard_audio" option there too,
on by default, as the OEM firmware of the ThinkCentre M920x offers in
its Devices menu ("Onboard Audio Controller").

TEST=Built lenovo/m920x, which offers it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/soc/intel/cannonlake/romstage/fsp_params.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/soc/intel/cannonlake/romstage/fsp_params.c b/src/soc/intel/cannonlake/romstage/fsp_params.c
index 9a9677bf55..b5c1b14641 100644
--- a/src/soc/intel/cannonlake/romstage/fsp_params.c
+++ b/src/soc/intel/cannonlake/romstage/fsp_params.c
@@ -95,7 +95,8 @@ void platform_fsp_memory_init_params_cb(FSPM_UPD *mupd, uint32_t version)
 
 	m_cfg->PchIshEnable = is_devfn_enabled(PCH_DEVFN_ISH);
 
-	m_cfg->PchHdaEnable = is_devfn_enabled(PCH_DEVFN_HDA);
+	/* The HD Audio controller, unless the "onboard_audio" option turns it off */
+	m_cfg->PchHdaEnable = is_devfn_enabled(PCH_DEVFN_HDA) && get_uint_option("onboard_audio", 1);
 
 	m_cfg->SaIpuEnable = is_devfn_enabled(SA_DEVFN_IPU);
 
